https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117868","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117868","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117868.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117868.patch","merged_at":"2026-04-01T18:03:19Z"},"body":"In theory, enabling eye-tracked foveated rendering (when it's available on the hardware) should always be a win, which is why we didn't originally add a setting for it.\r\n\r\nHowever, there is currently a bug in Pico's OpenXR runtime, where enabling it will cause a crash. It's Pico's bug and they'll fix it eventually, but in order to allow our users to work around it, this PR adds a setting for it which is enabled by default. This can allow developers to use feature tags to disable it on specific platforms, and then remove the workaround later after Pico fixes the underlying bug.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, foveation using Vulkan subsampled images should almost always be a win too, but we already added a setting for it, just in case. :-) This PR changes that setting to also be enabled by default","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view